Q3. Difference between Dependency Inversion
Principle (DIP) and Dependency Injection (DI)

Interview Ready Answer

Dependency Inversion Principle (DIP)

• Design Principle.
• High-Level modules depend on Abstractions.
• Reduces Coupling.
• Describes WHAT should happen.

------------------------------------------------------------

Dependency Injection (DI)

• Design Technique.
• Dependencies are provided from outside
  the class.
• Implements DIP.
• Describes HOW to achieve DIP.

------------------------------------------------------------

Without DI

class PaymentService{

    Payment payment=new StripePayment();
}

PaymentService creates its own dependency.

------------------------------------------------------------

With DI

Payment payment=new StripePayment();

PaymentService service=
new PaymentService(payment);

Dependency is created outside
and injected into the class.

Memory Trick

DIP

↓

Principle

↓

"What should happen?"

----------------------------

DI

↓

Technique

↓

"How to achieve it?"

